<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Virginia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Virginia is a region on the Atlantic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, named in honour of Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>. The colony founded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a> in 1607 was the first permanent English settlement in America. Its tobacco plantations, worked increasingly by enslaved Africans, made it a central part of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> in the Atlantic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virginia.jpg" alt="Virginia" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LadyofHats with additional editing by 痛 and Patrickneil / Charles Keck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Virginia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Setting</h2><p>Virginia, officially the Commonwealth of Virginia, lies between the Atlantic coast and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appalachian-mountains">Appalachian Mountains</a> and borders Kentucky, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>, North Carolina, West Virginia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>. Central Virginia lies mostly in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, the foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains, and the Shenandoah Valley holds the state's most productive farmland. Hampton Roads is the site of the region's main seaport and of Naval Station Norfolk.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">History</h2><p>Hunter-gatherers are estimated to have reached Virginia about 17,000 years ago, and Daugherty's Cave was in regular use as a rock shelter by 9,800 years ago. Farming spread in the late Woodland period, between 500 and 1000 CE. In the 1500s the native population within the present boundaries reached about 50,000. From the 1570s some thirty tribes of Tsenacommacah consolidated under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/powhatan">Wahunsenacawh</a>, commonly called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wahunsenacah">Chief Powhatan</a>, forming the Powhatan Confederacy, which governed more than 150 settlements with about 15,000 people in 1607. Three-quarters of the native population died of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> and other Old World diseases during that century.</p><p>In 1607 the London Company founded the Colony of Virginia, the first permanent English colony in the New World, which gave the state its nickname of the Old Dominion. Enslaved people from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and land taken from displaced native peoples fed the plantation economy and also fuelled conflict. The first General Assembly met in July 1619 and is the oldest lawmaking body in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. Virginians fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a> the state government in Richmond joined the Confederacy, while many north-western counties stayed loyal to the Union, which led to the separation of West Virginia in 1863.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">The place today</h2><p>The capital is Richmond and the most populous city is Virginia Beach; more than a third of the state's people live in Northern Virginia. The 2020 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/census">census</a> counted 8,631,393 residents. The state's motto is Sic Semper Tyrannis, Thus Always to Tyrants. Eight Virginians have been President of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, including four of the first five, which gave it the name Mother of Presidents. It is governed under its seventh constitution, approved in 1970.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Virginia” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The first permanent English settlement in the Americas came at Jamestown, <b>Virginia</b>, in 1607, a colony so precarious that the great majority of its settlers died during the “Starving Time” of 1609–1610.</blockquote><a href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Lincoln's call for 75,000 militia followed on 15 April, and <b>Virginia</b>, Arkansas, Tennessee and North Carolina seceded between April and May.</blockquote><a href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>From the late sixteenth century overseas trade expanded through chartered companies such as the East India Company, founded in 1600, and through colonies in North America and the Caribbean, beginning with Jamestown in <b>Virginia</b> in 1607.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-england">Kingdom of England · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Overseas commerce grew rapidly under the Navigation Acts, which reserved colonial trade for British ships: sugar from Jamaica and Barbados, tobacco from <b>Virginia</b> and Maryland and textiles from India were re-exported across Europe, and Glasgow prospered on tobacco after the union.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>The ‘20. and odd’ Africans landed in English <b>Virginia</b> in August 1619 were probably captives from Portuguese campaigns against Ndongo, shipped from Luanda on a slave ship bound for Veracruz.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-ndongo">Kingdom of Ndongo · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>Joseph Jenkins Roberts, a merchant born in <b>Virginia</b>, became the first president.</blockquote><a href="/empire/liberia">Liberia · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
